From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:40:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/cix: linlondp: don't warn about DPUs the firmware
 disabled

Every O6N boot logs at warning level:

  linlondp-cluster CIXH50C0:00: linlon-cluster: skip ACPI path "\_SB.DPU2", no physical node (trimmed?)
  linlondp-cluster CIXH50C0:00: linlon-cluster: skip ACPI path "\_SB.DPU3", no physical node (trimmed?)

The O6N firmware keeps all five CIXH5010 DPUs in the namespace and
returns _STA = 0 for DPU2 and DPU3. The board does not wire those pipes.
The ACPI core does not create a platform device for a device that is
not present, so these two never have a physical node. That is the
intended configuration, not a fault.

When the ACPI device is not present, log the skip at debug level and
call it "disabled by firmware". Keep the warning, without the guess, for
the case that really is unexpected: a present DPU with no platform
device. The child-walk variant of the same check gets the same
treatment.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor driver]
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 .../gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/linlondp_cluster.c  | 29 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/linlondp_cluster.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/linlondp_cluster.c
index 053f592c92de..f68e81845afb 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/linlondp_cluster.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/linlondp_cluster.c
@@ -232,9 +232,15 @@ static int linlondp_cluster_acpi_child_cb(struct acpi_device *child, void *data)
 
 	phys = acpi_get_first_physical_node(child);
 	if (!phys) {
-		dev_warn(ctx->cluster_dev,
-			 "ACPI cluster: skip child %s, no physical node (trimmed?)\n",
-			 dev_name(&child->dev));
+		/* A DPU the firmware disabled (_STA = 0) is expected. */
+		if (!child->status.present)
+			dev_dbg(ctx->cluster_dev,
+				"ACPI cluster: skip child %s, disabled by firmware\n",
+				dev_name(&child->dev));
+		else
+			dev_warn(ctx->cluster_dev,
+				 "ACPI cluster: skip child %s, no physical node\n",
+				 dev_name(&child->dev));
 		return 0;
 	}
 
@@ -320,9 +326,20 @@ static int linlondp_cluster_collect_dpus_acpi_paths(struct device *dev,
 
 		phys = acpi_get_first_physical_node(adev);
 		if (!phys) {
-			dev_warn(dev,
-				 "linlon-cluster: skip ACPI path \"%s\", no physical node (trimmed?)\n",
-				 path);
+			/*
+			 * Boards with fewer display pipes keep the DPU in the
+			 * namespace and disable it with _STA = 0 (O6N: DPU2 and
+			 * DPU3). Such a DPU never gets a platform device; that
+			 * is expected, not an error.
+			 */
+			if (!adev->status.present)
+				dev_dbg(dev,
+					"linlon-cluster: skip ACPI path \"%s\", disabled by firmware\n",
+					path);
+			else
+				dev_warn(dev,
+					 "linlon-cluster: skip ACPI path \"%s\", no physical node\n",
+					 path);
 			continue;
 		}
 
